---
import TimerPage from '@/layouts/TimerPage.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import { faqs } from '@/data/faqs';
import { relatedTimers, relatedPosts } from '@/data/related';
import { defaultConfigs } from '@/engine/presets';
import { meditations } from '@/data/meditations';
---

<TimerPage
  title="Meditation Timer – Interval Bells, Screen Stays On"
  description="Free meditation timer with gentle interval bells: 30 minutes with a soft bell every 10 by default, or any length you like. No ticking. Works offline."
  path="/meditation"
  h1="Meditation timer with interval bells"
  lede="This meditation timer keeps one clock for your whole sit. A soft bell can ring every 10 minutes, and one rings at the end. Nothing else makes a sound."
  config={defaultConfigs.meditation}
  faq={faqs['/meditation']}
  related={relatedTimers['/meditation']!}
  posts={relatedPosts['/meditation']}
  crumbName="Meditation timer"
>
  <Section title="How it's different" flush>
    <p>
      The other timers here are made to get your attention. This one is made to fade into the
      background. The big number shows the time left in the whole session. The quiet line under the
      bar shows the time to the next bell. Interval bells, the start bell and the end bell each have
      their own switch. So you can have one bell at the end and silence until then.
    </p>
    <p>
      The default is a 30 minute sit, with bells at 10 and 20 minutes and one to finish. That gives
      you three stretches of quiet. You might use them for a body scan, then the breath, then open
      awareness. Or they can simply be two gentle reminders to come back.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Presets">
    <p>Each length has its own page, with the bells already in place.</p>
    <ul class="links">
      {meditations.map((m) => (
        <li>
          <a href={m.path}>{m.h1}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Screen, sound, silence">
    <p>
      While the timer runs, it asks your phone or laptop to keep the screen awake. That way your sit
      doesn't end with a locked phone. If you'd like a dim room, turn the brightness down yourself.
      The bell is made right in your browser, so there's nothing to download. After your first
      visit, it works without a connection.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep this tab open and on screen. In a background tab, browsers slow timers down, so a bell
      can come late or not at all. With Sound off, phones that can vibrate (most Android phones)
      still buzz at each bell. iPhone browsers don't vibrate, so there Sound off gives you a silent
      sit.
    </p>
  </Section>
</TimerPage>
